ata-ref="d4d82dbd-39d2-47e1-a3bb-571a07fe4e70" data-undisplayed="undisplayed">Aim:</b><br data-ref="164ccc67-8598-4f57-beb4-beaa68a9abfd"><span class="question-text ql-editor" data-ref="1a55b00b-376a-43c5-89cd-94bdb540d63a"><p data-ref="850815e8-e17b-4c1e-8060-b9bb83d76b64" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0">Write a Python program that defines a base class <strong data-ref="155759b7-8276-4ab7-af72-e313655ba59d">Shape</strong> with two methods, <strong data-ref="1973e2b3-3b5e-44cd-981e-4f15c7501546">area</strong> and <strong data-ref="d06333e2-d3d2-4097-8374-8ba033ad6757">perimeter</strong>, that are meant to be overridden by subclasses. Define three subclasses: <strong data-ref="1248f21c-0080-4c9a-ba62-7165e6428fe3">Circle</strong>, <strong data-ref="2b9fc7f2-1541-459f-9e8e-0531a99bf7aa">Triangle</strong>, and <strong data-ref="3bbed8a8-57b7-47b7-a38a-859fff9883b4">Square</strong>, each of which implements the <strong data-ref="988e7799-e560-47cd-99fc-cb59cca1c2bf">area</strong> and <strong data-ref="41d0fbe0-e70e-4b5c-b323-32168b7777e8">perimeter</strong> methods. The program should then create instances of these subclasses based on user input and print their areas and perimeters, formatted to two decimal places.</p><p data-ref="10e0c7a9-4e38-4782-8a93-4de5f4f47603" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><br data-ref="a4c895b3-f6fc-44d1-af7e-a8cca5c49fc7"></p><p data-ref="05b066b0-35cc-40ac-a4fe-de5a523db03b" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><strong data-ref="e7a1df33-6ca2-4ed3-9726-79d5dcd03aec">Input Format:</strong></p><ul data-ref="27318fce-8b45-48f2-8e4e-bc0ced55ce22" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><li data-ref="b046152a-9ccd-4a71-b4e7-2e1bce389c63">The first line contains a single float representing the radius of a circle.</li><li data-ref="f0a72bcc-fa4c-4ccf-92ca-9a319453321d">The second line contains three space-separated floats representing the sides of a triangle.</li><li data-ref="d42bb681-0e38-4822-a510-f71cdfecefe5">The third line contains a single float representing the side length of a square.</li></ul><p data-ref="37549e31-d7ec-47db-b116-9e11dfcd53b5" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><br data-ref="b2e45629-2bc8-482f-9c39-58f61c44e7de"></p><p data-ref="0f2c8e97-34af-4e9d-8990-8f979836016f" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter